<title>USA: Genelabs to reveal GL701 results soon.</title>
<headline>Genelabs to reveal GL701 results soon.</headline>
<dateline>REDWOOD CITY, Calif 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Genelabs Technologies Inc said Thursday it intends to announce the preliminary results of its initial Phase III clinical trial for GL701 for lupus before the opening of Friday's market.</p>
<p>The company said it would not make any other statements before then.  </p>
<p>GL701, Genelabs' lead compound, is a pharmaceutical formulation containing the active ingredient dehydroepiandrosterone, or DHEA, a naturally occurring hormone produced by the adrenal glands. Lupus patients generally have abnormally low levels of DHEA.</p>
</text>
